- openregex 1.1.1 (edu.washington.cs.knowitall:openregex; LGPL, version 3 as its POM links it):
  https://github.com/knowitall/openregex
The LanguageTool language bundles it downloads (GitHub release languagetool-6.8.27 of this repository) are LanguageTool
6.8.27 language modules under the LGPL 2.1, built from https://github.com/JetBrains/languagetool. They also embed
dictionary data and libraries under other licenses, among them the GNU General Public License 2.0 and 3.0, the GNU
Lesser General Public License 2.1 and 3.0 and the Mozilla Public License 1.1 and 2.0: for example the Asturian, Catalan,
Irish, Italian, Galician, Khmer, Romanian and Tagalog dictionaries (GPL), the Spanish, Dutch, Portuguese, Ukrainian and
Swedish dictionaries and lucene-gosen (LGPL), and the French dictionary (MPL 2.0). The release notes of that release
(tools/languagetool-release-notes.md) list each component, its license and its upstream project, and the README and
license files of each dictionary are inside the bundle jars.
Phantom Code Coverage for Java (coverage/) packages JaCoCo 0.8.15 (org.jacoco:org.jacoco.*) under the Eclipse Public
License 2.0: https://github.com/jacoco/jacoco
The corresponding source code is attached to the GitHub releases that publish these files (tools/attach-sources.sh):
each release of these plugins and of the language bundles in this repository, and each release of
https://github.com/newkayak12/phantom-libs that carries these plugins for the Phantom IDE. It consists of the
-sources.jar files from the Maven repositories these libraries are published to and, for dictionary data published
without one, the upstream project or Hunspell files the data is built from. For three years after the last release
that contains them, Phantom contributors will also provide the complete corresponding source code of every component
named in this section, including all GPL, LGPL and MPL components of the language bundles, on a medium customarily
used for software interchange and for no more than the cost of providing it, to anyone who asks through
https://github.com/newkayak12/Phantom/issues.

